From: David Howells <dhowells@redhat.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:58:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] netfs: Fix netfs_read_to_pagecache() to pause on subreq
 failure

commit 8a8c0cfdf4658fc5b295b7fc87be56e0d76741f4 upstream.

[ Backport: drop the NETFS_RREQ_PAUSE wait. The 6.12 read collector never sets PAUSE and has no netfs_wait_for_paused_read(). ]
[ Backport: check NETFS_RREQ_FAILED at the common "done:" label. 6.12 issues each read source separately. ]

Fix netfs_read_to_pagecache() so that it pauses the generation of new
subrequests if an already-issued subrequest fails.

Fixes: ee4cdf7ba857 ("netfs: Speed up buffered reading")
Closes: https://sashiko.dev/#/patchset/20260425125426.3855807-1-dhowells%40redhat.com
Signed-off-by: David Howells <dhowells@redhat.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260512123404.719402-5-dhowells@redhat.com
cc: Paulo Alcantara <pc@manguebit.org>
cc: netfs@lists.linux.dev
cc: linux-fsdevel@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Christian Brauner <brauner@kernel.org>
---
 fs/netfs/buffered_read.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fs/netfs/buffered_read.c b/fs/netfs/buffered_read.c
index 68ad1ece65a0..692fa30ef5b1 100644
--- a/fs/netfs/buffered_read.c
+++ b/fs/netfs/buffered_read.c
@@ -285,6 +285,9 @@ static void netfs_read_to_pagecache(struct netfs_io_request *rreq)
 	done:
 		size -= slice;
 		start += slice;
+
+		if (test_bit(NETFS_RREQ_FAILED, &rreq->flags))
+			break;
 		cond_resched();
 	} while (size > 0);
 
